SUMMARY:ENS-Data Science colloquium – Alexander Mathis (EPFL) : Hierarchy
  and the body: what do multimodal models understand about behavior?
DESCRIPTION:| Behavior is how brains act on the world\, and measuring it pr
 ecisely is central to neuroscience\, medicine and many other fields. Deep 
 learning has made tracking bodies in video routine\, yet most behavioral m
 odels still map short clips to a fixed set of labels at a single timescale
 . This misses two defining properties of behavior. It is embodied: the bod
 y shapes how every action unfolds. And it…\nhttps://www.math.ens.psl.eu/
 evenement/ens-data-science-colloquium-alexander-mathis-epfl-hierarchy-and-
 the-body-what-do-multimodal-models-understand-about-behavior/
LOCATION:Amphi Jean Jaurès\, 29 rue d'Ulm\, 75005\, PARIS
URL:https://www.math.ens.psl.eu/evenement/ens-data-science-colloquium-alexa
 nder-mathis-epfl-hierarchy-and-the-body-what-do-multimodal-models-understa
 nd-about-behavior/
END:VEVENT
